<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Today's three slots.

     4×2 IS THE DESIGN, not a default to be tuned away. At 3×2 the card
     read as a note pinned to the home screen; the three things of the day
     deserve to hold their own against a wall of app icons, and this is the
     app's only surface that ever gets to. The extra WIDTH is what buys
     that — bigger type, the roman numerals, and titles that finish rather
     than truncate. All of it CampaignWidget derives from the slot it is
     actually given, so a resize changes the design rather than stretching
     it.

     Width earns more than height does, which is why this is 4×2 and not
     4×3: three rows of one-line titles is what the card has to show, and
     past about 190dp of height the extra space is air, not information. A
     drag upward is still worth making — at 3 cells the titles go to two
     lines — but that is a bonus for someone who wants it, not the default
     shape.

     minWidth/minHeight are the DEFAULT on API < 31, where targetCell* is
     ignored — 70·n − 30 gives 250dp for four columns and 110dp for two
     rows, so those devices open at 4×2 too rather than at some smaller
     size the layout was not drawn for.

     minResizeWidth lets a drag take it back to ~3 columns on a crowded
     home screen; below 240dp the numerals drop out, which is handled.
     minResizeHeight matches minHeight on purpose: the card can GROW
     vertically and use it, but three rows plus a header have nowhere to go
     below two cells.

     updatePeriodMillis is the system minimum, 30 minutes, and doubles as
     the midnight-rollover trigger. Every write pushes an update sooner —
     see GlanceWidgetRefresher. -->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="250dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="180dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="110dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="4"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="1800000"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:description="@string/widget_description" />
